# Security rules

Index: [docs/knowledge/security/README.md](../docs/knowledge/security/README.md)  
Auth detail: [auth-patterns](../skills/auth-patterns/SKILL.md)

## Secrets & environment

- ❌ Secrets, API keys, or private tokens in Client Components or client bundles
- ❌ `process.env.SECRET_*` referenced from `'use client'` modules
- ✅ Server-only env vars in Server Components, Server Actions, `app/api/**`, `core/config/env.ts`
- ✅ `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` only for values safe to expose to the browser

## Server Actions & route handlers

- Treat Server Actions like **public API endpoints** — authZ check inside the action/handler
- Validate all input with **Zod** before calling services
- Return safe error messages (i18n keys where applicable); no stack traces to clients

## Session & cookies

- Follow [auth-patterns](../skills/auth-patterns/SKILL.md) and [middleware-auth](../skills/auth-patterns/references/middleware-auth.md)
- Do not rely on middleware alone for authorization on mutations

## Client surface

- Avoid `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` unless sanitized; prefer framework-safe rendering
- CSRF: use framework defaults for Server Actions; for custom APIs verify origin/session

## Review

- Security-focused PR → [security-review](../skills/generators/security-review/SKILL.md) skill + **reviewer** agent last
